# Build context exclusions for the J1 controlled environment artifact.
#
# NOT AUTHORIZED. Nothing here builds anything.
#
# **This file is artifact-affecting and is a member of the build configuration
# manifest.** The Containerfile ends with `COPY . /opt/cardiosentinel/src-tree`,
# so whatever the build context contains ends up in a layer. Without this file
# the context is "whatever is in the runner's working directory", which is not
# the authorized source commit and is not the same twice.
#
# The specific defect this closes: `.git` is a directory of pack files whose
# bytes depend on when and how the repository was cloned. Two clean checkouts of
# the *same commit* routinely differ inside `.git`, so BUILD_A and BUILD_B would
# have diverged for a reason that has nothing to do with the environment being
# built -- and the two-build procedure would have reported a reproducibility
# failure about git's packing strategy.
#
# BuildKit resolves `<containerfile>.dockerignore` before `<context>/.dockerignore`,
# so this applies to this build and to no other.
#
# What is deliberately *not* excluded: `containers/j1-environment/requirements.*.txt`.
# The Containerfile copies them explicitly in an earlier layer, excluding them
# would break that COPY, and they are derived deterministically from the frozen
# lock -- they are build inputs, not context noise.

# Version control metadata. Not deterministic, not needed: the project version
# is static in pyproject.toml, so no build step reads git history.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Python build and test residue. Present or absent depending on what ran on the
# runner before the build, and byte-varying when present.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
build/
dist/
*.egg

# Virtual environments. Enormous, machine-specific, and never part of the image:
# the image installs the approved set from the derived dependency inputs.
.venv
venv
venvs

# Artifacts of this build procedure itself. Including a previous build's output
# in the next build's context is exactly the contamination the two-build
# independence rule exists to rule out.
*.oci.tar
build-a.json
build-b.json
j1-reproducibility.json
j1-qualification-claim.json

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
